-- the number of peaks a spectrum reports: the distinct shift values over a list of atoms. A shift
-- assignment that respects the symmetry gives equal values to atoms of one class, so the peak count is
-- the class count whenever distinct classes carry distinct values -- and less than it when they do not.
-- The count of classes is a fact about the molecule; the count of peaks is a fact about the molecule and
-- the instrument together.
peak-count : (A : Type 0) → (A → Nat) → List A → Nat
peak-count A sh xs = chem-length Nat (nub-by Nat eqb (chem-map A Nat sh xs))
